@prefix ds: <https://ds.canonical.com/>.
@prefix anatomy: <https://anatomy.canonical.com/>.
@prefix dt: <https://dt.canonical.com/>.

ds:global.subcomponent.chart_legend a ds:Subcomponent;
    ds:name "ChartLegend";
    ds:summary "";
    ds:anatomyDsl "---\n# TODO implementation: no reference in @canonical/react-ds-global or react-ds-global-form\n# Notation-only migration. Three repairs: the root uri was\n# `ds:global.component:ChartLegend` — the wrong type segment, the wrong block and\n# the retired colon spelling; the heading it referenced,\n# `ds:global.subcomponent:ChartLegendHeading`, names no ds: subject, so the\n# position becomes a role node; and the item reference is spelled as the subject\n# that does exist, global.subcomponent.chart_legend_item. The notation's markdown\n# fence and title line are dropped.\nnode:\n  uri: global.subcomponent.chart_legend\n  styles:\n    layout.type: flex\n    layout.direction: column\n    layout.align: flex-start\n  edges:\n    - node:\n        role: heading\n        styles:\n          # `text/secondary/bold` migrates to the composite it names; the size\n          # key admits dimension.* alone, so typography.font carries the tier.\n          typography.font: typography.text.secondary.bold\n          typography.color: color.text\n      relation:\n        cardinality: \"0..1\"\n        slotName: header\n    - node:\n        uri: global.subcomponent.chart_legend_item\n      relation:\n        cardinality: \"1..*\"\n        slotName: default";
    ds:anatomyClassic "";
    ds:usage "";
    ds:guidelines "**Accessibility**\n\n**Hover and focus triggers**  \nTooltips must be accessible via both pointer (hover) and keyboard (focus). Any element that triggers a tooltip must be focusable and expose the same information on focus as on hover. The tooltip itself has no focus state.\n\n**Screen reader support**  \nTooltip content should be programmatically associated with its trigger using appropriate ARIA attributes. Content must be announced without requiring additional interaction.\n\n**Content clarity and brevity**  \nAs mentioned earlier, tooltip content should be concise and written in plain language. Avoid relying on tooltips to communicate critical or required information, as they may not be consistently discovered.\n\n**Non-hover environments**  \nOn touch devices where hover is not available, tooltips should either appear on tap, or be replaced by an alternative pattern. Again, no essential info should be hidden behind a hover-only interaction. \n\n\n\n**Device and input considerations**\n\n**Pointer vs touch behavior**  \nOn pointer devices, tooltips appear on hover and dismiss on pointer exit. On touch devices, tooltips should be triggered by tap and dismissible via a second tap (on itself), outside tap, or timeout.\n\n**Target size and spacing**  \nInteractive elements that trigger tooltips must meet the minimum touch target size (24 px by 24 px on desktops). Avoid attaching tooltips to very small or densely packed targets without sufficient padding.\n\n**Responsive positioning**  \nTooltip placement should adapt to viewport constraints. When insufficient space is available, the tooltip should flip or reposition to remain fully visible.\n\n\n\n**Content**\n\n**Purpose of tooltips**  \nAgain, as mentioned earlier, use tooltips to provide supplementary, non-critical information that  is used as clarification.\n\n**Appropriate use cases**\n\n- Explaining unfamiliar icons, abbreviations, or controls\n- Providing short contextual hints without adding visual clutter\n- Supporting data interpretation in charts and dashboards\n\n**Avoid misuse**\n\n- Do not include essential instructions or required actions\n- Do not include complex, multi-step, or interactive content\n- Do not duplicate clearly visible labels or text\n\n**Length and structure**  \nKeep content short (ideally one line, maximum two lines for standard). Avoid paragraphs.\n\n\n\n**Animation**\n\n**Entrance and exit timing**  \nTooltips should appear after a short delay on hover or focus (~400 ms) and dismiss after a similar delay when the pointer leaves.\n\n**Motion behaviour**  \nThis element uses subtle, non-distracting motion. Cursor-follow behaviour (for data vis) should feel responsive and stable.\n\n**Interruptions and re-triggering**  \nIf the pointer moves between adjacent triggers, skip exit/entry animations and display the new tooltip immediately to maintain continuity.\n\n\n\n**Keyboard navigation**\n\n**Focus order**  \nTooltip triggers must be reachable via standard tab navigation. The tooltip itself should not receive focus unless it contains interactive content (which I realise can happen if we’re using links – could you help out here please [Elaine Liman](mailto:elaine.liman@canonical.com)?).\n\n**Dismissal**  \nTooltips should dismiss when the focus moves away from the trigger\n\n\n\n**Interaction behavior**\n\n**Trigger types**  \nTooltips may be triggered by icons, text, or UI controls. For data vis, tooltips may follow the cursor.\n\n**Positioning**  \nDefault placement should be centred relative to the trigger with a consistent offset. Placement should adjust dynamically to avoid viewport overflow.\n\n**Collision handling**  \nIn-built, but there is consistent collision padding to ensure tooltips do not touch screen edges (or overlap critical UI elements). \n\n\n\n**Layout and spacing**\n\n**Standard and dense variants**\n\n- Standard tooltips prioritise readability with balanced padding\n- Dense tooltips reduce spacing for compact environments\n\n\n\n**Wrapper variant**  \nWrapper tooltips support more complex content structures and flexible layouts. Spacing should follow token-based guidance but remain adaptable to context (at the designer’s discretion)\n\n\n\n**Color and theming**\n\n**Contrast and readability**  \nThe tooltip ensures sufficient contrast between its background and the text it houses, in all themes. \n\n**Contextual theming**  \nFor data vis, tooltip styling may match the visualisation theme (light or dark) for consistency.\n\n\n\n**Overflow and constraints**\n\n**Viewport boundaries**  \nTooltips must remain fully visible within the viewport. If necessary, reposition or constrain width.\n\n**Content overflow**  \nAvoid scrolling within tooltips. If content exceeds reasonable limits, use a more appropriate pattern (e.g.modal – do we have this?)";
    ds:tier ds:global;
    ds:parentComponent ds:global.component.data_tooltip;
    ds:hasTokenBinding [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.subcomponent.chart_legend;
        ds:node "$root/heading";
        anatomy:styleKey "typography.font";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:typography.text.secondary.bold
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.subcomponent.chart_legend;
        ds:node "$root/heading";
        anatomy:styleKey "typography.color";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:color.text
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.subcomponent.chart_legend_item;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "spacing.internal.block.start";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:dimension.100
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.subcomponent.chart_legend_item;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "spacing.internal.block.end";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:dimension.100
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.subcomponent.chart_legend_item;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "spacing.gap";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:dimension.100
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.subcomponent.chart_legend_item;
        ds:node "$root/marker";
        anatomy:styleKey "appearance.background";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:color.text
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.subcomponent.chart_legend_item;
        ds:node "$root/label";
        anatomy:styleKey "typography.font";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:typography.text.secondary
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.subcomponent.chart_legend_item;
        ds:node "$root/label";
        anatomy:styleKey "typography.color";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:color.text
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.subcomponent.chart_legend_item;
        ds:node "$root/value";
        anatomy:styleKey "typography.font";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:typography.text.secondary
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.subcomponent.chart_legend_item;
        ds:node "$root/value";
        anatomy:styleKey "typography.color";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:color.text
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global.subcomponent.chart_legend_item;
        ds:node "$root/divider";
        anatomy:styleKey "appearance.background";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:color.palette.gray.180
    ].
